{"nodes": [{"id": "core_actions_builtin_actions", "label": "Built-in actions (steps use/with/check model)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "core_actions_std_http_v1", "label": "std/http@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "core_actions_std_graphql_v1", "label": "std/graphql@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Validation failures (syntax, schema, unreadable query_file) fail the step before any request is made so the target never sees a malformed query; introspection fetch failure degrades to unvalidated runs rather than failing."}, {"id": "core_actions_std_tcp_v1", "label": "std/tcp@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "core_actions_std_udp_v1", "label": "std/udp@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TCP and UDP timing lands in http_req_duration alongside HTTP so percentiles are comparable across transports."}, {"id": "core_actions_std_pubsub_v1", "label": "std/pubsub@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When both publish and subscribe are given the subscription is established first, so a same-subject roundtrip sees its own messages."}, {"id": "core_actions_ws_family", "label": "WebSocket action family (std/ws@v1, std/ws-*@v1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ws-recv duration_ms deliberately does not feed http_req_duration: how long a server waits before pushing is not target latency and would poison the shared percentiles."}, {"id": "core_actions_grpc_family", "label": "gRPC action family (std/grpc@v1, std/grpc-*@v1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Calls are dynamic with no protobuf codegen \u2014 the schema arrives at run time via descriptor_set or reflection and requests/responses are JSON. Stream lifetimes span user steps, so streams deliberately do not feed grpc_req_duration (only unary calls do)."}, {"id": "core_actions_db_family", "label": "Database action family (std/db-*@v1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Queries run with unnamed statements so transaction-mode poolers (PgBouncer, Supabase Supavisor) are supported \u2014 a cached named statement would collide on the shared backend. Metric labels carry the step name only, never raw SQL; the DSN and its password are never logged."}, {"id": "core_actions_std_file_read_v1", "label": "std/file-read@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Process-wide cache revalidates against (mtime, size) on each access so a file edited between runs of a long-lived agent is picked up automatically; the cache saves disk reads, not the per-request copy."}, {"id": "core_actions_std_file_write_v1", "label": "std/file-write@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "core_actions_std_child_process_v1", "label": "std/child_process@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fail-closed: the run must opt in with allow_process_actions. Whatever is still alive at run end is stopped automatically (SIGTERM escalated to SIGKILL, whole process group) so a forgotten kill_process never leaks a server."}, {"id": "core_actions_std_kill_process_v1", "label": "std/kill_process@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stopping by registry name is preferred over a captured pid because pid/pgid/restart_count are a snapshot that moves on restarts."}, {"id": "core_actions_std_thresholds_v1", "label": "std/thresholds@v1 SLO gate action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Errors are hard: an unknown metric name, empty with, unparseable expression, or inapplicable aggregate fails the gate and the run \u2014 a broken gate never silently passes CI."}, {"id": "core_actions_std_check_v1", "label": "std/check@v1 assertion action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "message_* asserts use the any quantifier \u2014 at least one message must match, because streams carry noise (heartbeats, unrelated events)."}, {"id": "core_actions_std_sleep_v1", "label": "std/sleep@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "core_actions_std_log_v1", "label": "std/log@v1 action", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "core_actions_interpolation", "label": "Step interpolation (${{ }} placeholders and ${} generator tokens)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "${{ }} resolves once before the action runs while single-brace ${} tokens expand per execution/send; unknown names resolve to empty string and an unterminated ${{ is left as-is."}, {"id": "core_actions_action_handler", "label": "ActionHandler trait and register_action (downstream custom actions)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registered handlers are consulted only for action IDs no built-in std/* action matches, so built-ins pay no lookup cost; proprietary protocols like pro/fix@v1 plug in without a fork."}, {"id": "core_actions_actions_rs", "label": "crates/perfscale-core/src/step/actions.rs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "core_actions_safe_method_draft", "label": "draft-ietf-httpbis-safe-method-w-body (QUERY method)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/core/actions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-httpbis-safe-method-w-body/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "core_actions_std_pubsub_v1", "target":